# WS5-02/03/08 (DOS paths under vamos). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md (std.amiga.dos
# surface), dos.library autodocs (CreateDir returns a lock the caller must UnLock;
# Lock/UnLock pair; Examine with an allocated FileInfoBlock; CurrentDir returns the old
# lock, which the program must restore and the new one must be unlocked before exit).
# Expected: every call succeeds and nothing is left open or allocated at exit,
# including after setCurrentDir.
# Detector: probe.py --vamos-leaks fails an Amiga run whose vamos log reports a
# library or device left open ("can't expunge … open count") or orphan AllocMem
# memory (shown to fire on the seeded program 500-seeded-leak.c in the red check).
profiles: hosted-amiga-13 hosted-amiga
expect: output
contrast: let moved: bool = setCurrentDir("build"); ==> let moved: bool = true;
contrast-expect: output
--- output
true true true true true true
--- contrast-output
true true true true true true
